{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AAO RATING BADGE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Native replacement for the Loox "loox-rating" widget (the small stars + review count under a
product title on the PDP, and under the price on every collection card).

Two data sources, selected by snippets/aao-reviews-flags.liquid:

  json         legacy. Server-renders an empty span carrying the handle; assets/aao-reviews.js
               parses aao-reviews-summary.json ONCE per page and hydrates every badge from it.

  metaobjects  server-renders the stars and the count, no JavaScript involved.

********************************************
PERFORMANCE - why this does not average 124 reviews per card
********************************************

A collection page renders ~40 cards. Resolving a group's 124 `list.metaobject_reference` entries
and summing them once per card would be 40 x 124 = ~5,000 metaobject loads per page. So:

  * `aao_review_group` carries two derived fields, `rating_avg` and `rating_count`, written by the
    migration alongside the reviews. A badge pointing at a group reads those two fields and
    renders. Cost per card: ONE metaobject load, no list resolution, no loop. 40 cards on a
    collection page = 40 cheap reads, which is the same order as any other product metafield the
    card already reads.

  * `aao_own_reviews` products (11 of them, 1-3 reviews each) are summed inline. The list is tiny
    by construction and there is nothing to cache.

  * If a group's `rating_count` is blank - the client created a group by hand and did not fill the
    derived fields - the badge falls back to a hook (`data-aao-group`) instead of guessing. The
    expensive average is then computed exactly ONCE per page, in snippets/aao-reviews-boot.liquid,
    which walks only the groups that are actually missing their cache and publishes the result as
    window.AAO_REVIEW_STATS for assets/aao-reviews-mo.js to paint. Normal cost of that path: zero,
    because normally no group is missing its cache.

Net effect: the common path never loops.

And for any group over 50 reviews the cache is not an optimisation, it is the only correct source:
Liquid resolves at most 50 entries of a `list.metaobject_reference`, so the fallback compute
undercounts a 124-review group (it would read 50). Keep `rating_count` / `rating_avg` populated.
See docs/reviews/README.md, "The 50-reference cap".

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* product: the product whose rating to show. Required.
* link_to_reviews: when true, wrap the badge in an anchor to #aao-reviews (PDP use).
* hide_count: when true, show the stars only.
* show_empty: when true, keep the element in the layout for products with no reviews.
* style: optional extra inline CSS, e.g. 'margin-top:4px;'.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- capture bd_mode -%}{%- render 'aao-reviews-flags' -%}{%- endcapture -%}

{%- if product != blank -%}
  {%- capture aao_badge -%}
    {%- if bd_mode contains 'metaobjects' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign bd_own = product.metafields.custom.aao_own_reviews.value
        assign bd_group = product.metafields.custom.aao_review_group.value

        assign bd_avg = 0
        assign bd_count = 0
        assign bd_pending = ''

        if bd_own != blank and bd_own.size > 0
          assign bd_sum = 0
          for bd_r in bd_own
            if bd_r.hidden.value == true
              continue
            endif
            assign bd_count = bd_count | plus: 1
            assign bd_sum = bd_sum | plus: bd_r.rating.value
          endfor
          if bd_count > 0
            assign bd_avg = bd_sum | times: 10.0 | divided_by: bd_count | round | divided_by: 10.0
          endif
        elsif bd_group != blank
          assign bd_cached = bd_group.rating_count.value
          if bd_cached == blank
            assign bd_pending = bd_group.system.handle
          else
            assign bd_count = bd_cached
            assign bd_avg = bd_group.rating_avg.value | default: 0
          endif
        endif

        assign bd_show_count = true
        if hide_count
          assign bd_show_count = false
        endif
        assign bd_label = bd_avg | append: ' out of 5 stars'
      -%}

      {%- if bd_pending != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%} group with no derived cache: painted by assets/aao-reviews-mo.js {%- endcomment -%}
        <span
          class="aao-rating"
          data-aao-group="{{ bd_pending }}"
          {% if hide_count %}data-hide-count="true"{% endif %}
          {% if show_empty %}data-show-empty="true"{% endif %}
          {% if style != blank %}style="{{ style }}"{% endif %}
        ></span>
      {%- elsif bd_count > 0 -%}
        <span
          class="aao-rating"
          data-rating="{{ bd_avg }}"
          data-count="{{ bd_count }}"
          {% if style != blank %}style="{{ style }}"{% endif %}
        >
          {%- render 'aao-review-stars', rating: bd_avg, label: bd_label -%}
          {%- if bd_show_count -%}<span class="aao-rating__count">({{ bd_count }})</span>{%- endif -%}
        </span>
      {%- elsif show_empty -%}
        <span class="aao-rating"{% if style != blank %} style="{{ style }}"{% endif %}></span>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <span
        class="aao-rating"
        data-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
        data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
        {% if hide_count %}data-hide-count="true"{% endif %}
        {% if show_empty %}data-show-empty="true"{% endif %}
        {% if style != blank %}style="{{ style }}"{% endif %}
      ></span>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- assign aao_badge = aao_badge | strip -%}

  {%- if aao_badge != blank and link_to_reviews -%}
    <a href="#aao-reviews" class="aao-rating-link" aria-label="Scroll to reviews">{{ aao_badge }}</a>
  {%- else -%}
    {{ aao_badge }}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
